# 305 Starter Kit - Senior Architect Rules

## Core Technology Stack
- **Framework**: Next.js 15 (App Router, React 19).
- **Database**: Drizzle ORM with PostgreSQL (Supabase).
- **Authentication**: Supabase Auth (Server-side & Client-side).
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS with Shadcn/UI.
- **AI Integration**: Vercel AI SDK (Core, UI, and Streaming).
- **Payments**: Stripe (Subscription-based model).

## Architecture & Code Standards
- **Feature-Based Folder Structure**: Organize code by domain (e.g., `features/auth`, `features/billing`, `features/ai-agent`) instead of flat technical layers.
- **Server-First Approach**: Use React Server Components (RSC) by default. Use 'use client' only for interactive UI elements.
- **Server Actions**: Handle all data mutations via Server Actions with Zod validation. No custom API routes unless required for external webhooks.
- **Absolute Type Safety**: No 'any' type allowed. Use TypeScript interfaces and Zod schemas for all data models and action inputs.
- **Database Patterns**: Use a "Schema-first" modular approach. Split schema definitions in `lib/db/schema/`.
- **AI Implementation**: Follow Vercel AI SDK best practices. Separate AI logic from UI, utilize streaming responses, and implement robust error handling.

## UI/UX Standards (Miami Premium Style)
- **Theme**: Dark-first, professional, high-end.
- **Color Palette**: Backgrounds (Slate-950), Primary Accents (Gold/Turquoise), Success (Emerald).
- **Consistency**: Use Shadcn/UI components for all interactive elements.